# THIRD PARTY SOFTWARE NOTICES AND INFORMATION

Veyron OS is an original operating system written FROM SCRATCH in Rust and assembly.
It is NOT based on Linux, Android, BSD, Darwin, or any preexisting operating system kernel.

The following third-party components are allowed and catalogued below:

1. Limine Bootloader Protocol & EFI / BIOS binaries
   - Project: Limine Bootloader (https://github.com/limine-bootloader/limine)
   - License: 2-Clause BSD License
   - Usage: UEFI (`BOOTX64.EFI`) and BIOS stage loaders (`limine-bios.sys`) for booting the x86_64 higher-half ELF kernel.

2. wasm3 (WebAssembly Runtime)
   - Project: wasm3 (https://github.com/wasm3/wasm3)
   - License: MIT License
   - Usage: Embedded WebAssembly bytecode interpreter for running compiled portable binaries (including DOOM).

3. stb_truetype & stb_image
   - Author: Sean Barrett (stb libraries)
   - License: Public Domain / MIT Dual License
   - Usage: TrueType font vector rendering and image loading primitives.

4. BearSSL / mbedTLS
   - Project: BearSSL (https://bearssl.org) / mbedTLS
   - License: MIT License / Apache 2.0
   - Usage: Cryptographic TLS/SSL layer for HTTPS web requests over Veyron TCP/IP stack.

All other kernel subsystems (GDT, IDT, PIC, APIC, PIT, PMM, VMM, Kernel Heap, Scheduler,
Syscalls, AHCI SATA driver, ATA PIO driver, PS/2 Keyboard/Mouse drivers, PCI Bus Scanner,
FAT32 Filesystem, VFS abstraction layer, Fluent Compositor, Window Server, GUI Toolkit,
CMD Shell, File Explorer, Notepad, Paint, Calculator, Task Manager, Settings, and Native
TCP/IP Stack) are 100% original code written from scratch for Veyron OS.
